<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Thapsus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">46 BCE</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caesars-civil-war">Caesar's Civil War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Thapsus was fought on 6 April 46 BCE near Thapsus, on the coast of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunisia">Tunisia</a>, between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a> and the Pompeian forces of Metellus Scipio, supported by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juba-i">Juba I of Numidia</a>. Caesar's decisive victory destroyed the republican cause in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, and Cato, Juba and other leaders took their own lives. Caesar then annexed much of Numidia as the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa-nova">Africa Nova</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-thapsus.jpg" alt="Battle of Thapsus" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Thapsus,_46_BC_(Initial_deployment_of_troops).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
